            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Grapefruit Girl"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made so many changes I wasn't sure whether to write a review or a new recipe! First, I used fresh orange juice and plenty of orange zest. I replaced the prunes with dried apricots, halved the butter, and added honey. Tasted very good and orange-y."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I increase the servings to 12 portions and followed the quantities the recipe called for with a few changes:\nInstead of 4 cups orange juice I went with 3+1 cup of water.\nI added a teaspoon each of cumin and cinnamon and equal parts prunes and dried apricots. \nAfter simmering, I had a fair amount of liquid left so I used a spider to remove carrots and fruit and then turned up the heat to reduce liquid to a syrup. It was delicious and will definitely make again.",
            "datePublished": "2018-09-11T22:27:03.117Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Bsiegel"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I doubled the recipe for our Passover dinner. I used some prunes and apricots. I only used 1/2 of the orange juice and water for the rest. I could have used about 2/3 of the total liquid. Everyone loved it even those 2 who said they didn't like cooked carrots.",
            "datePublished": "2019-04-28T19:35:13.007Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ChemistryMama"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Solid starting recipe that is easy to adjust according to your own tastes. I used raisins instead of prunes and it came out great. If you are looking for a substitute for the fresh ginger, 1/8 tsp of ground dried ginger worked for me.",
            "datePublished": "2021-09-06T20:19:57.927Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
